  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed at the Gothic Theater on Saturday, September 16, 2017, delivering a two-hour set that spans their extensive catalog [1][2]. The concert opens with “The Young Thousands” from *We Shall All Be Healed* before moving into tracks like “Woke Up New” and “Unicorn Tolerance” [1]. The setlist includes material from albums such as *Goths*, *Heretic Pride*, and *The Sunset Tree*, alongside songs from *Black Pear Tree EP* and *Transcendental Youth* [1]. Notable tracks include “Elijah,” “San Bernardino,” and “Harlem Roulette,” which are part of the main set [1]. The performance concludes with a substantial encore featuring “Liza Forever Minnelli,” “Up the Wolves,” “This Year,” “You Were Cool,” “No Children,” “You Or Your Memory,” and “In The Craters On The Moon” [1][2]. This recording, captured by LMGBTapes, is the only available audio for this specific date in the archive [1][2]. The uploader notes that the audio was recorded using an iPhone 7 stored in a shirt pocket, despite the venue initially refusing equipment at the door [1]. The setlist contains twenty-one songs in total, with the final seven performed as encores [1][2]. This is the 238th archived show for the band, following a previous recording from June 2017 in Seattle [2]. Listeners can expect a comprehensive overview of the band’s work, from early releases to later albums, presented in a single continuous performance [1][2].",
